<%#
  The report widget's own settings form, and its empty state.

  `report_templates` is a LOCAL, handed in by whichever block partial rendered this, and
  since T-26a it comes from `WidgetReport.templates_for` — the same scope
  `WidgetReport.template_for` resolves against. One definition, so this form cannot offer
  a template the widget then refuses to render, which is the bug the base-plugin version's
  own comment described.

  THE EMPTY PICKER NEEDED A SENTENCE. With no usable template the two selects rendered as
  a blank dropdown and a Save button — a dead end with nothing saying why, and the two
  likeliest reasons (nobody has written a report template here yet; the project does not
  have the reports module enabled) are both things the reader can act on. `label_query`'s
  select is still shown, because a query is optional and the widget renders without one.
%>
<h3>
  <%= l(report_type == :issues ? :label_reporter_widget_report_by_issues
                              : :label_reporter_widget_report_by_spent_time) %>
</h3>

<div id="<%= block %>-settings">
  <% if report_templates.empty? %>
    <p class="nodata"><%= l(:text_reporter_widget_no_templates) %></p>
  <% else %>
    <%= form_tag(project_reporter_page_path(project, tab: tab.id), method: :patch, remote: true) do %>
      <div class="box report-settings">
        <p>
          <label>
            <%= l(:label_query) %>
            <%= select_tag "settings[#{block}][query_id]",
                           content_tag('option') + options_from_collection_for_select(queries, :id, :name, settings[:query_id]) %>
          </label>
          <label>
            <%= l(:label_reporter_report_template) %>
            <%= select_tag "settings[#{block}][report_template_id]",
                           content_tag('option') + options_from_collection_for_select(report_templates, :id, :name, settings[:report_template_id]) %>
          </label>
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        <%= submit_tag l(:button_save) %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
